'''Fuma Kotaro''' is an [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]] that can be obtained from the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[Sengoku Wargods Vajiras (Gacha Event)|Sengoku Wargods Vajiras]] gacha event. He was added in [[Version 15.2 Update|Version 15.2]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 850
|rarity = UR
|name1 = Fuma Kotaro
|name2 = Wargod Kotaro
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Wargod Kotaro''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
A backline crowd-controller for [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]], [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] and [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] enemies with a 100% chance to [[Slow]] targets for 3.17 seconds on average if both attacks land on the same enemy (at a 57% uptime). However, [[Explosion]]s can bring this up to over ~65% if it activates on his second hit.

Notably, his status as a backline rusher makes him a responsive unit in many stages against his targets, which are jam-packed with hyper-aggressive pushers all around. Though his uptime leaves much to be desired, he can hold [[St. Dober]]s and [[Winged Pigge]]s in place for other attackers, keep several [[Bore#Variants|Bore]] variants from wreaking too much havoc, or deal with overwhelming [[Angelic Gory|Angelic Gory]]/[[Shadow Boxer K]] spam, especially given the lingering hitboxes of his occasional Explosions catching incoming or rebounding enemies. However, this should not be relied on as a constant as Kotaro only has a 50% chance to trigger Explosions with each hit.

Kotaro's stats are generally sub-standard, having a very similar output to pre-TF [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Wolf]]—accounting for Explosion procs—while having a long cooldown on top of it. These stats are by no means terrible, and he gets the job done when it comes down to it, but his crowd-control should be the primary reason you use this Uber. Generally speaking, most non-Ubers options such as [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]] and [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] will suffice in handling these threats.

